# Parriwimple travelling with the party (docs/voice/parriwimple.md): short lines a guest says while walking with the party, shown and voiced
# like banter (story/banter.gd). The node's name says when it may play: quest_ on entering an area while their story is
# at that point (these come first), place_ on entering an area, fight_ after a won fight, idle_ now and then on the
# road. Each plays once per playthrough, only while Parriwimple is with the party. Every line here is unvoiced for now.

~ place_village
if guest:parriwimple and region:village_of_barovia
interject guest:parriwimple: That's Uncle's shop. He's counting the flour. Forty-one sacks. He'll know I'm gone by now.
endif
-> END

~ place_vallaki
if guest:parriwimple and region:vallaki
interject guest:parriwimple: So many houses. I counted to sixty and lost my place. I'll start again later.
endif
-> END

~ place_bonegrinder
if guest:parriwimple and region:old_bonegrinder
interject guest:parriwimple: The pie lady's windmill. It smells like bread. And like not bread. I don't want a pie.
endif
-> END

~ place_castle
if guest:parriwimple and region:castle_ravenloft
interject guest:parriwimple: That's a lot of stairs. I can carry anybody who gets tired. Even the ones in armour.
endif
-> END

~ fight_carry
if guest:parriwimple
interject guest:parriwimple: Is anybody hurt? I can carry you. I can carry two, if they're small.
endif
-> END

~ fight_uncle
if guest:parriwimple
interject guest:parriwimple: Uncle says not to fight. I didn't tell Uncle. I'm telling you.
endif
-> END

~ fight_none
if guest:parriwimple
interject guest:parriwimple: I counted them. All of them. Now there's none to count. That's the best number.
endif
-> END

~ idle_days
if guest:parriwimple
interject guest:parriwimple: I'm counting the days since we left the shop. I'll tell Uncle the number. He likes numbers better than people.
endif
-> END

~ idle_good_job
if guest:parriwimple
interject guest:parriwimple: Somebody told me I did a good job yesterday. I'm still thinking about it.
endif
-> END

~ idle_bread
if guest:parriwimple
interject guest:parriwimple: I carry bread to the lady with the empty house, every week. Don't tell Uncle. I'm telling you because you're kind.
endif
-> END
